# Control Design Decision Matrix

Before creating anything, ask: *What is the single responsibility?*

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Visual + state + templating | `TemplatedControl` (default) |
| Wrap single content | `ContentControl` |
| Display collection | `ItemsControl` / built-in list controls |
| Add interaction to existing control | Behavior |
| Cross-control layout hint | Attached property |
| Pure UI transform | Converter |
| Visual only | Style / ControlTheme override |

## Do NOT create a control when

Style, template override, behavior, or attached property is sufficient.

## Anti-patterns

- God controls mixing layout + data orchestration + state
- Feature flags (`IsCompact`, `EnableX`) — split into variants or composition
- Deep inheritance chains
- Business semantics in events (`CustomerSaved` → use UI events only)

## MVVM

Controls must support binding and commands without ViewModel-specific logic.

## Templates

- Document and validate `[TemplatePart]` parts in `OnApplyTemplate`
- Prefer `TemplateBinding`; avoid runtime visual tree search
